Z||000000||RiceCooker||05-27-2000||03:28 PM||||It was about this time last year that I took my newly acquired 86 SE to Montana for a liitle drive. (I wasn't on the forum so I'll tell ya all now) <BR>They had not speed limits and i heard they were puttin them back in so me and my pops decided to take a little performance ( high speed). <BR>So we get about 10 minutes inside the border and I start to see what she can do. As I get up to about 105-110 !!!PHWOUFFF!!! (great sound effects, eh) One of my headlight covers popped up and it scared the livin PISS out of me.<BR>I guess I better not write a novel here but this and the fact that I put her up to 5100 rpm in top gear (4spd) were the highlights of my day. I got up to 130 and ran right out of engine.<BR>This was one of the best days of my life and i guess i could tell you about the rest but i'll have to cut it short.<P>By the way, has anyone else's headlight covers popped up? Did you need to use toiletpaper afterwards too?||||reg||7
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-27-2000||04:09 PM||||You're car must be defective... My friends 86SE 3.1 swap got all the way up to 140mph before they popped up....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 05-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||05-27-2000||04:51 PM||||Ahh, the old Montanabahn.  When I moved from WA to CT a few years ago, my wife was chasing in her T-bird Super Coupe.  It was nice to open it up in between mounain ranges.  We both saw 120 a couple of times. Roof out, windows down, and no headlight popup problems.<p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 05-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||olympic||05-27-2000||11:32 PM||||Ricecooker,<BR>  Thats one reason you'll see some Fiero owners have installed vents in the hood of their car.  The vents help reduce the air pressure under the hood at high speed and prevent the headlights from popping up.  The vents also aid in removing hot air from behind the radiator.||||reg||1
